====================================================================================
  (1/k)C(k,j) - (1/j)C(k-1,j-1)  simplify -> 0
  numeric summand identity: 429 (j,k) pairs, mismatches = 0
  numeric  sum_(k=j)^m (1/k)C(k,j) = C(m,j)/j : 429 (j,m) pairs, mismatches = 0
  numeric hockey stick  sum_(l=j-1)^(m-1) C(l,j-1) = C(m,j): mismatches = 0

====================================================================================
ITEM 3c -- does the CRUDE bound really produce a log n?  (constructed independently)
====================================================================================
  crude:   |R(m)| <= sum_{k=j}^{m} 1 * E/(k n^2) = (E/n^2) * (H_m - H_{j-1})
  exact :  |R(m)| <= (E/n^2) * (1/(C(m,j))) * sum_{k=j}^m C(k,j)/k = E/(j n^2)

    j    m=n   crude factor (H_m-H_(j-1))   exact factor 1/j  crude/exact
    1     10                     2.928968           1.000000        2.929
    1    100                     5.187378           1.000000        5.187
    1   1000                     7.485471           1.000000        7.485
    1  10000                     9.787606           1.000000        9.788
    1 100000                    12.090146           1.000000       12.090
    3     10                     1.428968           0.333333        4.287
    3    100                     3.687378           0.333333       11.062
    3   1000                     5.985471           0.333333       17.956
    3  10000                     8.287606           0.333333       24.863
    3 100000                    10.590146           0.333333       31.770
    6     10                     0.645635           0.166667        3.874
    6    100                     2.904044           0.166667       17.424
    6   1000                     5.202138           0.166667       31.213
    6  10000                     7.504273           0.166667       45.026
    6 100000                     9.806813           0.166667       58.841

  crude factor grows like log n (H_n ~ ln n + gamma);  exact factor is the
  constant 1/j.  So the document's claim that exact telescoping removes a
  spurious log n that the crude bound would introduce is CORRECT, not overstated.
  (check: H_100000 = 12.09015, ln(100000)+gamma = 12.09014)
